q q .780392 .823529 .870588 RG .5 w 56.69291 796.5354 m 538.5827 796.5354 l S .333333 .333333 .333333 rg BT 9.6 TL/F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.69291 807.874 Tm (RUNGTA INTERNATIONAL SKILLS UNIVERSITY)Tj T* ET 56.69291 42.51969 m 538.5827 42.51969 l S BT 1 0 0 1 295.4138 25.51181 Tm T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 749.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 21 TL/F2 17 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (1. ABSTRACT)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 693.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .22671 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm <54686520456c6563747269636974792042696c6c2043616c63756c61746f72206973206120736d616c6c20507974686f6e2070726f6772616d20707265706172656420746f2063616c63756c617465206120636f6e73756d6572927320656c6563747269636974792062696c6c2066726f6d>Tj T* 1.501254 Tw (the number of units used. The bill is calculated using three electricity-rate slabs, a fixed charge and a tax)Tj T* 0 Tw <616d6f756e742e205468652070726f6772616d20616c736f2061736b7320666f722074686520636f6e73756d65729273206e616d6520616e6420646973706c6179732074686520726573756c7420696e2061206e6561742062696c6c20666f726d61742e>Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 643.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .023584 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (The problem addressed by this project is the repeated manual calculation of electricity charges. When different)Tj T* -.121844 Tw (rates are applied to different ranges of units, it can be easy to make a calculation mistake. This program follows)Tj T* 0 Tw (the given slab rules and performs the calculation automatically.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 593.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .485664 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (The program is written in Python 3. It uses input statements, conditional statements, arithmetic operators and)Tj T* .62091 Tw (user-defined functions. A try-except block is also used so that non-numeric unit input can be handled without)Tj T* 0 Tw (stopping the program unexpectedly.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 543.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 2.122144 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (The current version covers the requirements given in Project Statement No. 89. It calculates the energy)Tj T* 1.139293 Tw (charge, adds the fixed charge of Rs. 50, calculates tax at 5% on the energy charge plus fixed charge, and)Tj T* 0 Tw (prints the total bill. It also checks that the entered units are not negative.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 520.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 15 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm (Expected outcome)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 472.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT -.11169 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (The expected outcome is a simple and understandable program that gives the correct bill for normal, boundary,)Tj T* 2.192544 Tw (higher-unit and invalid-input cases. It can be used as a basic example of applying Python programming)Tj T* 0 Tw (concepts to a practical calculation problem.)Tj T* ET Q Q

