q q .780392 .823529 .870588 RG .5 w 56.69291 796.5354 m 538.5827 796.5354 l S .333333 .333333 .333333 rg BT 9.6 TL/F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.69291 807.874 Tm (RUNGTA INTERNATIONAL SKILLS UNIVERSITY)Tj T* ET 56.69291 42.51969 m 538.5827 42.51969 l S BT 1 0 0 1 295.4138 25.51181 Tm T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 749.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 21 TL/F2 17 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (2. INTRODUCTION)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 679.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.28424 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 46.4 Tm (Python is a high-level programming language that is commonly used for learning programming and solving)Tj T* .923448 Tw (everyday problems. Its syntax is easy to read, so a beginner can focus on the logic of a problem instead of)Tj T* .476197 Tw (spending too much time on complicated language rules. Python supports conditions, functions and operators,)Tj T* 0 Tw (which are useful for building this project.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 656.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 15 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm (Background)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 608.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .434054 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (Electricity consumers are charged according to the number of units they use. In this project, the charge is not)Tj T* 1.295448 Tw (the same for every unit. The first 100 units have one rate, the next 100 units have another rate, and units)Tj T* 0 Tw (above 200 have a higher rate. A fixed charge and tax are also added to the bill.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 585.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 15 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm (Problem statement)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 537.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 2.48871 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (Write a Python 3 program that takes the consumer name and units consumed as input, calculates the)Tj T* .848454 Tw (electricity energy charge using the given slabs, adds a fixed charge and tax, and prints a formatted bill. The)Tj T* 0 Tw (program must use if-elif-else for slab-wise calculation and functions for organising the work.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 514.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 15 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm (Motivation)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 466.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .05811 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (The main motivation for choosing this problem is that it connects programming concepts with a familiar real-life)Tj T* .48951 Tw (activity. It gives practice in breaking a problem into smaller steps, checking conditions and testing the answer)Tj T* 0 Tw (with different inputs.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 443.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 15 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm (Slab rates used in this project)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 77.95276 329.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg 0 108 439.3701 -18 re f* 1 1 1 rg 0 90 439.3701 -18 re f* .952941 .964706 .980392 rg 0 72 439.3701 -18 re f* 1 1 1 rg 0 54 439.3701 -18 re f* .952941 .964706 .980392 rg 0 36 439.3701 -18 re f* 1 1 1 rg 0 18 439.3701 -18 re f* BT 12 TL/F2 8.8 Tf 1 0 0 1 6 96.2 Tm (Unit range)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 218.5984 96.2 Tm (Rate)Tj T* ET 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 8.8 Tf 1 0 0 1 6 78.2 Tm (First 100 units)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 218.5984 78.2 Tm (Rs. 3 per unit)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 6 60.2 Tm <4e6578742031303020756e69747320283130319632303029>Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 218.5984 60.2 Tm (Rs. 5 per unit)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 6 42.2 Tm (Above 200 units)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 218.5984 42.2 Tm (Rs. 8 per unit)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 6 24.2 Tm (Fixed charge)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 218.5984 24.2 Tm (Rs. 50)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 6 6.2 Tm (Tax)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 218.5984 6.2 Tm (5% of \(energy charge + fixed charge\))Tj T* ET q .666667 .717647 .768627 RG 1 J 1 j .5 w 0 108 m 439.3701 108 l S 0 0 m 439.3701 0 l S 0 0 m 0 108 l S 439.3701 0 m 439.3701 108 l S 0 90 m 439.3701 90 l S 0 72 m 439.3701 72 l S 0 54 m 439.3701 54 l S 0 36 m 439.3701 36 l S 0 18 m 439.3701 18 l S 212.5984 0 m 212.5984 108 l S Q Q Q

