e above 200, charge Rs. 3 for the first 100, Rs. 5 for the next 100 and Rs. 8 for the remaining units.)Tj T* 0 Tw (9. Add the fixed charge of Rs. 50.)Tj T* (10. Calculate tax at 5% of energy charge plus fixed charge.)Tj T* (11. Calculate the total bill and print the bill.)Tj T* (12. Stop.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 388.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 15 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm (Coding, testing and debugging)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 340.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .87856 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (The calculation is placed in a separate function so that the slab logic is not repeated in the main part of the)Tj T* -.041873 Tw (program. A second function prepares and prints the bill. The program is then run with normal, boundary, invalid)Tj T* 0 Tw (and above-200-unit inputs. The output is compared with the expected values given in the question.)Tj T* ET Q Q

