ete electricity bill.)Tj T* <506172616d65746572733a206e616d65209620636f6e73756d6572206e616d653b20756e6974732096206e756d626572206f6620756e69747320636f6e73756d65642e>Tj T* (Return value: This function prints the bill and does not return a calculated value.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 465.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .68871 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (Working: It calls calculate_energy_charge\(units\), sets the fixed charge to Rs. 50, calculates tax as 5% of the)Tj T* .382409 Tw (energy charge plus fixed charge, adds all amounts to get the total bill and prints the details using two decimal)Tj T* 0 Tw (places.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 442.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 15 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm (How the functions work together)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 394.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .790488 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.4 Tm (The main part of the program accepts the input and checks whether it is valid. When the units are valid and)Tj T* .82868 Tw (non-negative, it calls generate_bill\(\). That function calls calculate_energy_charge\(\) to get the energy charge.)Tj T* 0 Tw (After receiving the returned amount, it completes the remaining calculations and prints the bill.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 371.6929 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 15 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm (Function flow)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 337.6929 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 2.311724 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 18.4 Tm (Main program )Tj/F3 9.6 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.6 Tf ( validate units )Tj/F3 9.6 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.6 Tf ( generate_bill\(name, units\) )Tj/F3 9.6 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.6 Tf ( calculate_energy_charge\(units\) )Tj/F3 9.6 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.6 Tf ( return)Tj T* 0 Tw (energy charge )Tj/F3 9.6 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.6 Tf ( calculate tax and total )Tj/F3 9.6 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.6 Tf ( print bill.)Tj T* ET Q Q

